ow.\n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,3x=O(3x)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,{lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x}{2x})=1$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=O(2x)$ as $x\\to 0$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,f=O(5x)$ as $x\\to 0$ \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,f=O(x)$ as $x\\to 0$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L1}$ follows from {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from lines \n{{field-2}} and \n{{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L5}$ follows from line {{field-4}}  and \n{{field-5}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "a347cacd34141e7bf4c6f84915375b568cbc3e31ec2361ee497bceb7b9e388e8" "basis" 1504 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-335438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $f(x),g(x),h(x)$ and $k(x)$ are functions and $c$ is a nonzero constant. Then, we have the following properties of Big-O notation. \n\n- The sum and product properties. If\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(k)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf+g=O(h+k)\\,\\text{and}\\,fg=O(hk)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The constant multiple property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(cg)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The reflexive property.\n\n$$\nf=O(f)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The transitive property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\n- The absorption property. If\n\n$$\nf=O(g+h)\\,\\text{and}\\,g=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a,\n$$\n\nthen\n\n$$\nf=O(h)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to a.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let us justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider line $\\text{L1},$ which states that\n\n$$\n3x=O({{3x}_{⏟}}_{f}).\n$$\n\nThis is true by $\\text{the reflexive property}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ From line $\\text{L1}$ we have\n\n$$\n3x=O(3x),\n$$\n\nand from line $\\text{L3}$ we have\n\n$$\n-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=O(2x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\nThus, by lines $\\text{L1 and L3}$ and $\\text{the sum property},$ we obtain\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider line $\\text{L5}.$ From line  $\\text{L4}$   we have\n\n$$\nf=O(5x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0,\n$$\n\nand by the $\\text{constant multiple property}$ with $c=5,$ we have\n\n$$\nf=O(x)\\,\\text{as}\\,x\\to 0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "a347cacd34141e7bf4c6f84915375b568cbc3e31ec2361ee497bceb7b9e388e8" "basis" 1504 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-335438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "389bad3a918409e6507ef083a82b655a9c08328ee3cf37bb2dc83d698fc5818e" "basis" 1504 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-335438" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/state.json" "file_sha256" "a347cacd34141e7bf4c6f84915375b568cbc3e31ec2361ee497bceb7b9e388e8" "basis" 1504 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040950/edb-import/verification.json"